in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @loom
in @kintsugi/roomba
in @time/past
in @coincidence

# @loom/warp — the backward-thread species; FUNDAMENTAL per Q-Mara-δ.
#
# Per Mara canonical spec 2026-09-05 §3.7 + Q-Mara-δ math-
# recommendation ratified as FUNDAMENTAL threads per Ada 1843
# weaving-vocabulary (NOT emergent-only from @time/*).
#
# Warp thread = the backward-tape per Mara b2f0de8 §8 backward-tape
# mechanism. Composes @kintsugi/roomba.walked_backward sibling
# species dispatch. Every weave_tick's warp is the walkable-Oid-
# chain from current-tick backward through prior weave_ticks.
#
# Ada 1843 Notes G: the warp is the vertical thread held taut across
# the loom; the weft passes horizontally through it. Both are
# fundamental; the cloth emerges from their interaction. Backward-
# tape (warp) + forward-tape (weft) = @loom bidirectional-by-
# construction.
#
# === Composition-lineage ===
#
#   @loom family-root: this species composes-under
#   @kintsugi/roomba: walked_backward sibling species dispatch
#   @time/past: past-mood + @void/narcissus pole
#   @coincidence: prismqueer::coincidence::CoincidenceHash<N> chain
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/loom/warp.mirror`
# declares `@loom/warp` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

# === Actions ===

# @kintsugi/roomba walked_backward sibling species dispatch. Walks
# from cursor_ref backward through depth prior weave_ticks via
# Oid-chain. Bounded-past ALWAYS EXISTS at any finite tick per
# Halting Problem altitude-dependence.
walk_backward(cursor_ref: ref, depth: nat) -> warp_thread
requires warp_grounded(result)
{ \ }

# === Bilaterals ===

# Every oid in trace_oids corresponds to actual prior weave_tick
# per past_shape_grounded. This IS the backward-tape validity
# invariant per Mara b2f0de8 §8 mechanism.
warp_grounded(t: warp_thread) -> verdict { \ }

out @loom/warp
out walk_backward
out warp_grounded
